mc_p1="Stuart McGill, a spine biomechanist (Spine Biomechanics Laboratory, University of Waterloo), is a highly influential author in practice. His approach is an author's proposal, not a guideline recommendation.",
mc_p2="Verifiable example: McGill and Karpowicz 2009 used surface EMG and 3D analysis to quantify variants of the curl up, side bridge and bird dog in 8 healthy men, to guide starting level, progression, dosage and corrective technique. These are the three exercises popularly called the “Big 3”. It is basic science, not a patient trial.",
